# Angular inputs and Tailwind classes

## Signal inputs belong on the `@Component` class

Do not put `input()` / `input.required()` only on a base `@Directive()` that the component extends. The Angular language service often reports NG8002 ("Can't bind to 'x'") for inherited signal inputs even when runtime works.

```typescript
// Wrong — LS may not see image on ecomm-product-card-desktop
@Directive()
export class ProductCardBaseDirective {
  readonly image = input('');
}
@Component({ selector: 'ecomm-product-card-desktop', ... })
export class ProductCardDesktopComponent extends ProductCardBaseDirective {}

// Right — inputs on the component (match ecomm-button)
@Component({ selector: 'ecomm-product-card-desktop', ... })
export class ProductCardDesktopComponent {
  readonly image = input('');
}
```

Shared behaviour: extract helpers/functions, or duplicate small `input()`/`computed()` blocks on desktop and mobile components. Prefer the same pattern as `ButtonComponent` / `StatusPillComponent`.

Before binding a new `[prop]` in an app template, confirm that prop is declared with `input()` on the imported component class itself (not only a base directive).

## Desktop/mobile base classes

For app `*BaseDirective` classes shared by desktop/mobile components: prefer a **plain TypeScript class** (no `@Directive()`) when the base only holds `inject()` / signals / methods. Empty `@Directive()` bases often make the language service report NG8002 / “property does not exist” on the subclass template even though `ng build` is clean.

Keep `[formGroup]` on a `<form>` (or an element that ReactiveFormsModule clearly owns), and import `ReactiveFormsModule` on the concrete `@Component`.

## Prefer canonical Tailwind utilities

When Tailwind IntelliSense suggests a canonical class (`suggestCanonicalClasses`), use it.

- Prefer `min-w-180` over `min-w-[720px]` (divide px by 4 for the spacing scale)
- Prefer `z-70` over `z-[70]`, `z-60` over `z-[60]`
- Prefer `max-w-62.5` over `max-w-[250px]` when it matches the scale

Keep arbitrary values only when there is no scale token (unusual colours, one-off shadows, complex animations). Do not expand every `text-[13px]` in the repo unless IntelliSense flags it and a project token exists.
